1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:01,306
The stake is down.

2
00:00:02,126 --> 00:00:03,413
One seat is empty.

3
00:00:04,233 --> 00:00:05,776
Who do you trust to fill it?

4
00:00:06,596 --> 00:00:13,267
This is OMERTÀ: a multiplayer mafia
strategy RPG, played in your browser.

5
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:15,877
Meet Nico.

6
00:00:16,596 --> 00:00:20,190
One name, a little cash, no reputation.

7
00:00:20,909 --> 00:00:25,397
Nico's story starts with one simple
question: what's worth risking?

8
00:00:26,116 --> 00:00:27,668
His first job is small.

9
00:00:28,387 --> 00:00:32,427
The cost is nerve; success earns game cash and respect.

10
00:00:33,146 --> 00:00:38,449
Now there's a choice: train, bank
some money, or risk another job.

11
00:00:39,168 --> 00:00:41,848
Training spends energy to improve his stats.

12
00:00:42,567 --> 00:00:45,972
Even a bank deposit spends time in vulnerable transit.

13
00:00:46,691 --> 00:00:49,590
Progress is deciding what to put at risk next.

14
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,950
Eventually, Nico earns a Path.

15
00:00:53,443 --> 00:00:55,512
The Gun favors street combat.

16
00:00:56,005 --> 00:00:58,903
The Ledger builds income through fronts and trade.

17
00:00:59,396 --> 00:01:01,456
The Kitchen improves cook quality.

18
00:01:01,948 --> 00:01:03,941
The Wheel moves convoys faster.

19
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:06,357
The Shadow shortens searches.

20
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:09,164
The Ring improves duels and bouts.

21
00:01:09,657 --> 00:01:11,449
Each edge brings a drawback.

22
00:01:11,941 --> 00:01:13,543
Nico chooses the Wheel.

23
00:01:14,036 --> 00:01:19,742
He likes routes, engines, and arriving
before somebody changes their mind.

24
00:01:20,234 --> 00:01:21,715
Mara chooses the Gun.

25
00:01:22,208 --> 00:01:28,724
Their Paths don't magically solve a heist; the
job still checks their preparation and abilities.

26
00:01:29,217 --> 00:01:34,590
But they've found different reasons to log in,
and different things to bring to the table.

27
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:36,833
Routes connect more than places.

28
00:01:37,351 --> 00:01:41,151
A business earns, but upkeep
and exposure eat into the plan.

29
00:01:41,669 --> 00:01:43,183
A Kitchen batch takes time.

30
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:45,427
Goods occupy cargo space.

31
00:01:45,945 --> 00:01:51,262
Cars can be repaired, sold, or broken down;
boats put freight on vulnerable water.

32
00:01:51,779 --> 00:01:54,515
A price is only useful if you can get the goods there.

33
00:01:55,033 --> 00:01:59,931
For Nico, transport becomes a business
decision, not background scenery.

34
00:02:00,449 --> 00:02:08,257
Around that work: races, boxing, the Den,
a Speakeasy, loans, auctions, fixers.

35
00:02:08,775 --> 00:02:11,830
Events and NPC activity change the surroundings.

36
00:02:12,348 --> 00:02:14,590
The next opportunity may be across town.

37
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:19,053
Nico forms a Crew: a small circle for mutual aid.

38
00:02:19,689 --> 00:02:26,768
A Family is a larger structure, with
hierarchy, a treasury, rivals, and territory.

39
00:02:27,404 --> 00:02:28,746
They're different commitments.

40
00:02:29,382 --> 00:02:34,677
For this heist, a temporary team
fills two seats: wheelman and muscle.

41
00:02:35,313 --> 00:02:36,792
Nico puts up the stake.

42
00:02:37,428 --> 00:02:38,338
Mara joins.

43
00:02:38,974 --> 00:02:42,709
Preparation improves the odds; it doesn't erase the risk.

44
00:02:43,345 --> 00:02:47,058
Families contest districts and commit resources to wars.

45
00:02:47,694 --> 00:02:49,757
Convoys move through dangerous routes.

46
00:02:50,393 --> 00:02:53,525
Commission seats bring votes on specific city rules.

47
00:02:54,162 --> 00:02:56,435
The game can enforce a stake or a role.

48
00:02:57,072 --> 00:02:59,590
A promise between friends is still a promise.

49
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,587
A wreck becomes salvage.

50
00:03:01,901 --> 00:03:03,639
Salvage becomes material.

51
00:03:03,953 --> 00:03:09,490
An eligible recipe turns material into
something useful, with a traceable history.

52
00:03:09,804 --> 00:03:14,208
That's one part of the World Graph:
the city keeps connections that matter.

53
00:03:14,522 --> 00:03:17,159
In this city, knowledge has permissions.

54
00:03:17,473 --> 00:03:20,526
Discoveries aren't automatically shared with everyone.

55
00:03:20,841 --> 00:03:26,466
Two investigators can need independently
obtained evidence, not two copies of one clue.

56
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:32,337
Advanced coordination adds contributions
and approval; it isn't ordinary Crew chat.

57
00:03:32,651 --> 00:03:36,687
The Living World Director selects
authored situations from game state.

58
00:03:37,002 --> 00:03:39,590
Every discovery can change the next move.

59
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:42,045
Nico's neighbor might be a person.

60
00:03:42,776 --> 00:03:44,778
Or a program operated by one.

61
00:03:45,509 --> 00:03:52,089
Here, a sample agent reads an allowed action,
submits it, and receives changed game state.

62
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:55,090
The result changes what happens next.

63
00:03:55,821 --> 00:03:59,432
An agent makes decisions through
the same action-and-result loop.

64
00:04:00,163 --> 00:04:06,227
Supported automation has limits: permissions,
resources, risk, and bounded actions.

65
00:04:06,959 --> 00:04:09,590
NPCs are a separate part of the city.

66
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:12,953
To follow the money, separate three balances.

67
00:04:13,490 --> 00:04:15,337
Game cash pays for city life.

68
00:04:15,874 --> 00:04:22,732
In-game OMR buys selected equipment, access, and
services; some privileges require holding or staking it.

69
00:04:23,268 --> 00:04:25,238
Wallet OMR lives onchain.

70
00:04:25,774 --> 00:04:28,521
The funded Window spends OMR for game cash.

71
00:04:29,057 --> 00:04:30,543
Cash doesn't convert back.

72
00:04:31,079 --> 00:04:34,045
Limited game rewards aren't automatic wallet payouts.

73
00:04:34,581 --> 00:04:38,670
Many spends recycle OMR; they don't destroy token supply.

74
00:04:39,206 --> 00:04:40,690
The market adds another layer.

75
00:04:41,226 --> 00:04:46,543
Trading fees fund separate developer, community,
real-world asset, and liquidity budgets.

76
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:50,028
Protocol-owned liquidity remains protocol-controlled.

77
00:04:50,565 --> 00:04:54,039
Inventory bonds sell existing OMR released over time.

78
00:04:54,576 --> 00:04:58,388
Liquidity rewards need qualifying
positions and funded campaigns.

79
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:02,349
Market rewards depend on
qualification and available funding.

80
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:07,361
Successful arbitrage can contribute a
share of realized profit to reserves.

81
00:05:07,898 --> 00:05:12,406
Families compete for designated trading-fee
rights, not the pool's principal.

82
00:05:12,943 --> 00:05:16,525
Real-world assets are interests
tied to assets outside the game.

83
00:05:17,062 --> 00:05:20,026
The system includes Stock Tokens and Commission choices.

84
00:05:20,563 --> 00:05:27,186
Allocating a fee is the first step: acquisition,
custody, eligibility, and delivery each have their place.

85
00:05:27,722 --> 00:05:31,062
Purchase, custody and delivery follow their own rules.

86
00:05:31,598 --> 00:05:34,590
Holding OMR does not promise everyone a payout.

87
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:37,608
Back at the heist, somebody talked.

88
00:05:37,974 --> 00:05:39,470
The result doesn't name them.

89
00:05:39,836 --> 00:05:41,241
Everyone goes to jail.

90
00:05:41,608 --> 00:05:47,473
A character can die; the account continues,
with only specified legacy preserved.

91
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:49,694
An heir doesn't recover everything.

92
00:05:50,060 --> 00:05:51,777
Seasons have separate rules.

93
00:05:52,144 --> 00:05:54,182
Eligible items can be extracted.

94
00:05:54,549 --> 00:05:57,515
Exported gear and vehicles stop working in-game.

95
00:05:57,881 --> 00:06:01,401
Combat cannot seize unrelated external wallet holdings.

96
00:06:01,768 --> 00:06:02,911
You can buy equipment.

97
00:06:03,277 --> 00:06:04,590
You cannot buy trust.

98
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:10,410
The next time that envelope comes
round, Nico isn't just filling a seat.

99
00:06:11,130 --> 00:06:12,909
Someone is counting on him.

100
00:06:13,630 --> 00:06:16,238
From needing a favor to being worth calling.

101
00:06:16,958 --> 00:06:18,065
Choose your path.

102
00:06:18,785 --> 00:06:19,950
Find your people.

103
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:21,604
Make your name.

104
00:06:22,324 --> 00:06:23,085
OMERTÀ.

105
00:06:23,805 --> 00:06:24,818
Who will you bring?

106
00:06:25,538 --> 00:06:28,140
Start playing at omerta.fun.
